dust, and blood you'll see in this book was made by hand. The artist iezeradd spent a month creating a library of custom textures for us to construct the book from. The design is meant to echo old editions while simultaneously looking like something that was discovered rotting in the woods. This is as much a love letter to the game as it is a demonstration you don't need a lot of money, nor AI to make something beautiful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T14:15:10-07:00","id":1540100,"title":"","content":"Looks awesome, can't wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T14:35:43-07:00","id":1540101,"title":"","content":"It looks beautiful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T14:55:20-07:00","id":1540102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1540090#post1540090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow! That's petty awesome! Thanks for the preview!</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll be in touch again soon! Your work on the Dead Mountain sheet was stellar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T15:51:32-07:00","id":1540105,"title":"","content":"I know it's a bit hypocritical of me to say this, but can't this cause some problems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T16:30:29-07:00","id":1540108,"title":"","content":"It would definitely cause problems if this were a corebook, which this is not. This book nor any books in the series will enable a standalone game. Much like the Savage Age players guides, you still need a corebook to play fully. It's best thought of as a quickstart meant to streamline and simplify the availability of information to run people through early stories with enemies and protags up through rank 3 in this book, and additional ranks and power levels of play in successive releases. The team are being quite careful to remain within STV's community content guidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T05:00:48-07:00","id":1540126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1540102#post1540102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll be in touch again soon! Your work on the Dead Mountain sheet was stellar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool, thanks! I'll be looking forward to it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And glad you were happy with the Dead Mountain sheet, I thought that turned out really good too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T10:37:39-07:00","id":1540132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1540108#post1540108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would definitely cause problems if this were a corebook, which this is not. This book nor any books in the series will enable a standalone game. Much like the Savage Age players guides, you still need a corebook to play fully. It's best thought of as a quickstart meant to streamline and simplify the availability of information to run people through early stories with enemies and protags up through rank 3 in this book, and additional ranks and power levels of play in successive releases. The team are being quite careful to remain within STV's community content guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it demand an edition in particular, or is it compatible with both W20 and W5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T15:17:49-07:00","id":1540146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1540132#post1540132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it demand an edition in particular, or is it compatible with both W20 and W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are not attempting to rewrite the W5 canon 1:1 but this setting is a suitable alternative hitting all the critical notes in the meta. This series is presented as edition holistic and should be equally comfortable across all editions of Werewolf: the Apocalypse (sans MET) with ample translation tools. If one has a W5 corebook and wanted to run a WtE game they should be able to. That said our direct citations heavily favor Revised and W20, giving both equal regard in endnotes whenever it pertains to a corebook specifically. A scenario where players have W5 corebooks and an ST with older editions for deep lore dives wouldn't be unusual at a WtE table, especially if they find the players want more than what w5's meta offers.<br /> <br /> Off the table talk, we're all big fans of Revised mechanics married with the BNS werewolf meta but understand most younger fans use the W20 books. That said revised books on PoD over at DTRPG are cheaper than W20 by a surprising margin, so we're citing them both out of hopes people will come to embrace revised as a viable edition when considering buying into one or the other.<br /> <br /> Our approach has been to have our resident researcher, ExcelGarou, pull all data from a given subject across all WtA books put to print to find which takes are the most comprehensive and fit the best in our meta. That'll eventually become our citations we use when referring Storytellers to deeper lore on any on given topic. In cases where we don't have a solid 1:1 citation and are exploring more generalized info for presenting unique game content we'll make a sort of amalgamation across all the editions to build a more generalized vibe of a given subject.<br /> <br /> Short answer, either corebook, W5 or W20, should be usable with WtE, but W20 will have a leg up when it comes to mechanics crunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T22:43:04-07:00","id":1540413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1540089#post1540089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to offer an idea what Werewolf the Essentials is;<b> It takes the divided Nation from the BNS WtA book and builds upon it.</b> It includes the Bitten, but so they do not override other breeds.<br /> <br /> The focus, as a direct challenge to W5, is of community and unity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, the bolded sentence is the aspect I find the most fascinating about WtE.<br /> <br /> Like from what little read about the East and West Concordats, I got the impression that the interactions tend to be more civil than say the Sabbat and Camilla in the sense that they won't default trying to kill each other on sight since the reason the Concordats because the circumstances are purely political instead of an ancient blood feud like say the pure and the forsaken. Which is kinda novel when it comes to the usual interactions between factions in a WoD product.<br /> <br /> And honestly I think it has the potential to tell some interesting stories and present some interesting moral dilemmas to the player.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-15-2024, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T18:41:24-07:00","id":1541373,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/GFY6Ybs.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/GFY6Ybs.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/GFY6Ybs.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bnY6Xd8.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/bnY6Xd8.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/bnY6Xd8.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/HJoctN2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/HJoctN2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/HJoctN2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/760449490611240960/project-update-090124?source=share\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/0105726eb5408e66720c7f3dad137521/87e7d9c41004e773-0f/s640x960/1354703e9827bf3a438f61dd4073be31bb87a9b4.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/760449490611240960/project-update-090124?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> Post by @songoftrillium &middot; 2 images </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/760449490611240960/project-update-090124?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/760449490611240960/project-update-090124?source=share </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 0&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 46&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 92&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Project Update 09/01/24&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Hello, Kinfolks. We're a little under 60 days from releasing Book 1: Cliath, and I wanted to give you all a quick update, provide a few book facts, and&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> So the Main author for the WtE project just posted an update for the project that's mainly centred around the payment plans for all the people who worked on the book and how it would affect the final price and a preview of the opening comic for this book.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Also as bonus here's the write-up for the Get of Fenris<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3RMPCh2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3RMPCh2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3RMPCh2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/stKbAmj.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/stKbAmj.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/stKbAmj.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/iGKmomt.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/iGKmomt.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/iGKmomt.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/i4XViEs.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/i4XViEs.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/i4XViEs.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T03:21:07-07:00","id":1541439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1541228-w5-shattered-nation-review?p=1541436#post1541436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forgetting is only the first part that is so baffling. Because the follow-up is also the implication that after the knowledge of the history has been forgotten throughout generations, the response to that was these newer Garou supposedly thinking &quot;What happened back then...? I dunno.&quot;. And then they just moved on! Even some of the most ancient human cultures already cared about memorializing their past in some fashion (like having a tradition of oral storytelling). Even if it isn't 100% the truth, you'd think they would come up with some sort of story they could look at as a documentation of their shared history. But what W5 is suggesting is that after the amnesia, there was simply no attempt to create any sort of history for themselves. &quot;The Garou Nation? Dunno what that was... was it a decade? A century? A millenia? Who knows.&quot;. That sort of ambivalence would only make sense if these newer Garou stopped caring altogether about being a Garou and didn't identify like that anymore.<br /> <br /> And you see that in the Legendary Rites. They are all these recent events (although of course according to Shattered Nation, the 80s and 90s are already &quot;ancient history&quot;). There's no creation-myth of Garou interacting with Gaia and Luna for the first time, no Rite about the Impergium and the Concord or any myths about how these Tribes with their respective Patron Spirits came to be... It's all just shrugged off in favor of more recent stuff. You'd think the most prevalent Legendary Rites would be these events that are fundamental to the Garou's sense of history and identity rather than having a Rite about one Garou's adventures from a couple of years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>So about W5's total apathy towards history could be explained by this post by mundis on Tumblr:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can definitely see that. Even the 'twisted upbringing flaw' reflects exactly that: a Garou who was only offered a highly distorted view of the Garou and needs to undergo extensive deprogramming.<br /> <br /> Playing with the 'unreality' idea of the W5 universe crossing over to WtE, there's a Pentex version of Werewolf: the Apocalypse they put out that almost hilariously features a lot of aspects of the w5 verse. Imagine a game setting where Pentex did, in fact, release their version of Werewolf (Lycanthrope: the Rapture). Canonically it was never released, but maybe in an alt universe iIt became a household name like D&amp;D. Suddenly, you have a fuckton of Lost Cubs who believe that game world is real and begin reaching out to work with the makers (the 'fuck everyone' elders of w5) who are looking to trap the players in increasingly amoral missions until it becomes imperative for the player characters to go 'no fucking way' and start looking around themselves with the intention to see through the ruse (and you'd have to work with the players that they expect the subversion.)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Black Dog</b> is a division of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pentex\" target=\"_blank\">Pentex</a>, and produces <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Roleplaying_game_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">roleplaying games</a>. They're best known for their <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Talespinner_System\" target=\"_blank\">Talespinner System</a> games set in the Romantic-Rage setting of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Shadow\" target=\"_blank\">World of Shadow</a>. Black Dog affect that their games are much cooler than other RPGs, because they're not geek romps through Arthurian landscapes or nerdy interstellar politics, but set in the modern era. In truth, most of their plots and characters are lifted directly from Terry Brooks novels and <i>Star Trek</i>. <i>As the </i><i><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Glass_Walkers\" target=\"_blank\">Glass Walkers</a></i><i> fall to the </i><i><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wyrm\" target=\"_blank\">Wyrm</a></i><i>, and they follow the dictates of the </i><i><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pentex\" target=\"_blank\">Pentex</a></i><i> Corporate Father, one of their tasks is to get published a </i><i><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Time_of_Judgment\" target=\"_blank\">catastrophic series of events</a></i><i> in Black Dog's major game lines.</i></div> \u200b </div> </div> </div>:<br /> <br /> TlDR: It's a mass Gaslighting effort by pentex aimed at Lost Cubs with the purpose of misleading them and possibly set them on the path of the black spiral. Hence the total dismissal of garou history. <br /> <br /> At least that's how mundus would integrate W5's lore into WtE if they're forced to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T23:54:04-07:00","id":1542031,"title":"","content":"And... how WtE Garou gonna interact with other splats. Esp with vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T21:40:57-07:00","id":1542091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542031#post1542031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... how WtE Garou gonna interact with other splats. Esp with vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well from what I've seen it varies on the tribal alliance. For the West concordat, it would probably be some variation of kill on sight. So basically business as usual. While for East it depends on a vampire. Like a high humanity, caitiff fleeing from the clutches of the camellia will garner plenty of sympathy from them while a low humanity Sabbat elder who starve they underlings so they become wrights won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T00:06:10-07:00","id":1542100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542031#post1542031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... how WtE Garou gonna interact with other splats. Esp with vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends entirely on how you define a vampire. Suppose we're talking in the Slavic sense. In that case, everything is some kind of vampire, and werewolves are theoretically also vampires, up there with cats, ghosts, and people who don't eat their vegetables. In that context, Werewolf: the Essentials will be an <i>excellent</i> vampire game. /j <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If we're talking in terms of how well it plays with Vampire: the Masquerade, 5th edition Werewolf is <i>definitely</i> the superior choice in Werewolf editions that mesh best with V:tM if you want werewolves meant to be played like V:tM.<br /> <br /> But joking aside, I don't have a meaningful answer to the question because the two splats were never meant to go toe-to-toe with the other (not that combat was ever a central point to WoD games anyway.) so I can't tell you if this is going to play well with Vampire. The play style, power level, and even the pathos of the two games are mutually incompatible beyond a surface-level integration (Under a Blood Red Moon being the exception rather than the rule.) Of course, ultimately, what matters is if the ST and players are having fun, so I suppose if you want an excellent vampire experience that meshes with werewolves, any enterprising Storyteller with the chutzpah can make it happen regardless of edition.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry I have nothing more substantive to offer you there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T22:11:20-07:00","id":1542351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542100#post1542100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SNIP</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about relationships between splats...<br /> <br /> How would you characterise the relationship between the Western and Eastern Concordats?<br /> <br /> Like from what I've seen the antagonism between them isn't as bad as say the Pure and Forsaken. At worst it's more of a cold war situation where conflict between the alliances takes the from of spy games and back room deals with open combat between the two sides usually limited to formal duels. And the conflict between the Concordats are usually the concern of the elders leading both sides while individual pack are more welling to get along.<br /> <br /> At least that's my conclusion on the conflict between the alliances from what little I've seen in the preview material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T22:46:18-07:00","id":1542353,"title":"","content":"Well, from my tumbler reading, they both have the same goals ( broadly speaking) they just have different ways of arriving at them....so they're not even as far apart as human political parties for the most part. They strike me more as Hard Left vs Soft Left.......they both want to shut down the puppy farm......but one is lobbying hard and sending dozens of Animal Welfare inspectors the other snuck in at night with a half dozen pickups and does a hard entry search and seizure home invasion...and possibly accidentally sets off a gas explosion as they leave...<br /> <br /> Jobs done either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Ok, just realised this is basically also Cult of Fenris vs Gaian activities in W5........and whilst the former has likely more widespread positive flowthrough its very slow.....the other just feels a lot more satisfying and is immediately if somewhat limited in its usefulness....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 09-18-2024, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T00:47:02-07:00","id":1542357,"title":"","content":"So, there are three factions in this first book outlined thus far\u2014four if you consider the unaffiliated Red Talons and Silent Striders.<ul><li><b>Western Concordat</b> \u2014Your garden variety Garou Nation outlook, traditions, and organization. Their interests are primarily centered around the usual song and dance of direct action in opposition to the Wyrm, a largely antagonistic perspective on the Weaver, and a very Calvinist kind of purity philosophy concerning social politics. They are much more attuned to understanding Harano and believe unity is what will drive it off. They think if the Tribes unify, Gaia will reawaken. They are all about reunification and reinforcing the traditions that have always stood. They're facing the reality they can't entirely afford to use Cliath as the cannon fodder they once were; there just aren't enough nowadays to do things the old way.</li> <li><b>Eastern Concorda</b>t \u2014 Highly humanized and rapidly coming to embrace the trappings of civilization\u2014with caveats. They believe that if they heal the world and the destroyed Caerns, Gaia will follow and heal with them. They are best attuned towards rebuilding and reconstruction of the wreckage left by the Storm Eater. Many of their efforts are centered around building and nourishing Shard Caerns and covertly converting the population towards being better stewards of the world. In short, their society is in a 'post-war rebuild' mindset. They think a corrupt human society started it, and a healed and Gaian human society will fix it. They embrace Bitten far more than the other factions.</li> <li><b>Dawn Tribes </b>\u2014 The revivalists of Turtle Island and Abya Yala hold a widely varied number of stances, but at its core sits the belief that this is not the first Apocalypse but one of many, having occurred to many societies and civilizations in the Dawn Tribes and that the end has come for the Garou Nation as well. To them, this is the age of the Fifth Sun. Unlike the other factions, they believe all three of the triat are vital and must be disentangled from one another. Of all the factions, they are all the most aligned towards spiritually decolonizing the nations and their homes. They were handling the Wyrm perfectly well before the Wyrmcomers arrived, and want a return of their precolonial traditions. They embrace their kin and crinos more than the others.</li> </ul>When push comes to shove, all three will go to war when the Wyrm shows its face and will aid one another (in each tribes' way, good luck convincing the Balam to do it any way other than their own.) They all follow The Litany, at least by their interpretations of it. Regarding the Council of Tribes and the higher ranks, you can find much room for cloak and dagger kind of cold war conflict. I think that the higher the Garou rank, the more entrenched they are in a social conflict between factions, but Damian has it right when push comes to shove. Packs that were together before the nation fractured are still together, and they're like:<br /> <br /> &quot;My dad said we're enemies now.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah. Wanna go kill this Black Spiral pack?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd think of it a lot less like a cold war between countries and more of a messy, ongoing divorce between people who still love one another; they argue over pets and cars and housewares, but what they really want is eachother. If you want to know some direct inspiration, I listened to the new Sufjan Stevens album Javelin while doing the primary writing for the factions. Eastern Concordat is &quot;Shit Talk,&quot; Dawn Tribes are &quot;Goodbye Evergreen,&quot; and Westcons are &quot;So You Are Tired.&quot; People understand their hands are tied mainly in tribe Politics, but everyone is still willing to work together, short of their main differences. The Westcons are unlikely ever to treat their kin and crinos entirely the same as the other factions and still hold a more conservative view of charachs. There will be dynamics where faction influence ought to have a major say in any given sept's overall policies and disposition. When the unified fight ends though, many of the old wounds still remain. An excellent approach to viewing the factions here is that the things that motivate them to action are a strong defining point of unity.<br /> <br /> Once thing to pay attention to when you do read the chapter on the tribes is the opening passage for each of them, which I'm calling their Call to Action. That is something that, at its core, defines what the tribe does both in its faction and abroad. It is sorta like the 'verbs' but in a more pathologized format. The same goes for Gifts too. What your character stands for more defines the Gifts they'll have access to than their XP or freebie allocations, breed, auspice, tribe, or even the faction they're a part of.<br /> <br /> Rage asks the Killi &quot;When Will You Rage?&quot;<br /> Gnosis asks the Killi &quot;What Do You Stand For?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T01:23:12-07:00","id":1542358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542353#post1542353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *Ok, just realised this is basically also Cult of Fenris vs Gaian activities in W5........and whilst the former has likely more widespread positive flowthrough its very slow.....the other just feels a lot more satisfying and is immediately if somewhat limited in its usefulness....</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is ironic since Get of Fenris is the tribe that's the most likely to get along with Eastan Concordat since they are the only tribe in the Western Concordat that don't have any hangups with the Kinfolk and as written they won't turn away the help from fellow warriors of Gaia for something petty as politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T07:24:41-07:00","id":1542366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542357#post1542357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there are three factions in this first book outlined thus far\u2014four if you consider the unaffiliated Red Talons and Silent Striders.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what are the Red Talons doing? I can guess what the Silent Striders are doing--trying to act as neutral messengers and go-betweens. But while it makes sense why the Talons wouldn't want to work with any of those factions, I can't come up with a good guess on what they intend on doing next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T12:03:55-07:00","id":1542380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542366#post1542366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are the Red Talons doing? I can guess what the Silent Striders are doing--trying to act as neutral messengers and go-betweens. But while it makes sense why the Talons wouldn't want to work with any of those factions, I can't come up with a good guess on what they intend on doing next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do what they've always done, but now without any oversight from the Nation. Essentially, they are wolves first and as wolves don't have nation the Talons don't, either.<br /> <br /> That is to say, they continue to put their fingers in their ears about the need to make actual choices that aren't related to being a wolf. They didn't as much cede from the Nation as they refused to pick a side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T16:10:54-07:00","id":1542399,"title":"","content":"Yeah, its more or less as Ana Mizuki puts it, and you're right about the striders staying adamantly neutral to keep the lines of communication open. The idea of the Red Talons being organized feels too human to me (and the idea of them in prior editions deferring to a kingly figure feels silly.) This isn't to say they don't have septs or sept roles, but when seen from the outside, they're almost indistinguishable from a Yellowstone superpack, minus the shapeshifting and violence that often follows their revels, and propensity for fighting the Wyrm. It wasn't that they refused to join the council of tribes or any one faction; they've no emissaries capable of speaking for the entire tribe.<br /> <br /> I've written them as a Tribe that doesn't even entirely identify as a Tribe, at least in the same way the other Tribes think of it. They are better seen here as an autonomous collective of mostly unaffiliated all-wolf septs. I've written them presented as a tribe that didn't come together. Instead, Griffin sought out, handpicked, and convinced them of his politics long ago, spreading and coalescing a &quot;You and I are wolves, but we are not the same.&quot; mindset throughout these previously uncontacted lupus septs. From there, it spread to known septs, and the Talons began effectively taking Lupus from other tribes, taking off in greater numbers around the Dark Ages (see Red Talons and Older/Younger Brother.) A tribe that grew memetically through shared unexpressed grief at a world that is increasingly shrinking, along with their families and loved ones. A significant reason the tribe persists is the continuation of the tradition of Griffin convincing lupus of other tribes to join his cause. Their extreme position is one they arrived at through desperation rather than an organized decision.<br /> <br /> I tweaked their history a little to make them a little more playable and a lot more relatable. They never even named themselves Red Talons, nor did they agree to the accords, but rather, a single lupus that didn't claim membership to anything called a tribe showed up, declared &quot;I am a wolf like you, we are all wolves.&quot; When pressed to name their tribe, paired with increasing frustrations between the exchanges, the Garou finally lashed out and was like, &quot;You want to know what I am? This is what I am!&quot; and clawed the other Garou, meeting the demand with three bloody gashes before leaving, earning wolves like that one the label of Red Talon. Gifts, rites, and traditions remain more or less the same here; otherwise, they are just a bit more tragic and narratively sensical for an all-wolf tribe. In WtE, they start out of the running gates with being the one tribe out of them all with no more caerns of their own, having lost them at the apex of the Age of Apocalypse. This puts them into an existential crisis of facing extinction for learning how to compromise and work with other Tribes to learn and start building their own Shard Caerns, creating divisions within the &quot;Tribe&quot; itself.<br /> <br /> Additionally, with homids facing a declining population for the first time, this has created a talking point for the two to relate better to one another. This unknown position they're in and the direction it goes is ultimately for the tabletop to decide. In the long term, I'm hoping it steers in the direction of 'growing pangs towards something greater,' but not all tables are likely to play it like that.<br /> <br /> When the Nation split, they initially joined the Western Concordat. When the Glass Walkers quit the eastern concordat and joined the westcons it so thoroughly alienated the Red Talons that they dropped what tenuous affiliations they once had altogether. This outcome is one that's driven mixed opinions between tribes. On one hand, they are losing potential allies. On the other hand, with the Red Talons out of the Western Concordat, the faction is a lot less likely to trend towards extremism, leading some to think the Glass Walkers scoffing at the Eastcons' acceptance of the Hearthbound and joining the Westcons may have been a political maneuver catalyzed by the Shadow Lords to shift the Overton Window away from extremism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T04:05:11-07:00","id":1542478,"title":"","content":"So J. F. Sambrano just posted about one of his lore contribution to the WtE project on his Patreon for anybody who wants to set aside $5 USD a month. It seems to be a write-up for the<a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/balam-werewolf-112406438?utm_medium=clipboard_copy&amp;utm_source=copyLink&amp;utm_campaign=postshare_fan&amp;utm_content=web_share\" target=\"_blank\"> Balam/werejaguars</a> of the Dawn Tribes. Also he has written two lore posts for his <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/posts/extinction-echo-108333286?utm_medium=clipboard_copy&amp;utm_source=copyLink&amp;utm_campaign=postshare_fan&amp;utm_content=web_share\" target=\"_blank\">Extinction </a>Project and one of them' free so you guys can have a sneak preview of that and see if you want to support him..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T17:34:52-07:00","id":1542846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542399#post1542399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In WtE, they start out of the running gates with being the one tribe out of them all with no more caerns of their own, having lost them at the apex of the Age of Apocalypse. This puts them into an existential crisis of facing extinction for learning how to compromise and work with other Tribes to learn and start building their own Shard Caerns, creating divisions within the &quot;Tribe&quot; itself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about caerns I wonder hard it is to actually make new ones? I'm not really an expert on caern building rules but I've heard it's easy as buring a piont of gnosis for minor caerns at least. Though from what I've read of the preview material it seemes the apocalypse rendered the old ways of creating useless or at least too difficult to be worth it in most situations and the only reliable way to acally make a caern is to use a shard seed which is apparently in limited supply and the tribe that has the knowledge to make them belongs to the eastern concordat which the Shadowlords are more than welling to use as leverage ageist the Western concordant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-29-2024, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T01:35:57-07:00","id":1542859,"title":"","content":"The old Caern-building rites have effectively become bane-summoning rites from start to finish, making the creation of new caerns (called Great Caerns in this setting) more or less impossible. A shard caern is so-named after its heart, which is little more than a spiritual sliver taken from the heart of one of the 13 remaining Great Caerns. They are weaker and far more vulnerable to attack but retain the same abilities and powers reflecting the Great Caern that provided the shard.<br /> <br /> Kahaila, the Native American Ao, have returned. With the awakening of Turtle came their reawakening with it, each of them following a dream that jolted each of them awake of Gaia's Heart, a long-extinct gnostic flower believed to bridge the physical and spiritual world naturally. They, in turn, began seeking and awakening Hatha, Native American black bears of the Dawn Tribes who possess the means to heal the land and bring fossilized flora and fauna back to life. The Gurahl understood their duty from Gaia as her healers and began reluctantly restoring communication with both the Dawn Tribes and the Children of Gaia. Margrave Josef Konietzko saw an opportunity to form a new faction, and while other tribes were still reeling from the Sundering of their Caerns, threw the full might of the Shadow Lords' support behind the Children of Gaia to launch a go-for-broke expedition deep into Pangaea to recover a specimen of this plant.<br /> <br /> In short, they succeeded. They recovered the flower, a trillium-like plant called Gaia's Heart, from fossils from the Middle Devonian Epoch, when bones first appeared. This is from a time when Gaia was so powerful; she held an omniscient awareness of her realm, and the entire Gaian Realm was as spiritually charged as a caern, held together in a fine mycelial network connecting these delicate plants. Even in Pangaea, they managed to recover a single fossilized specimen. It was enough. They were able to bring it back to life, and upon planting it on a Great Caern's bawn and carefully tending it with ancient rites, it bloomed and began producing Shard Seeds.<br /> <br /> When planted and cared for in this manner, Shard Seeds produce more Gaia's Heart flowers. When grown in a cleansed and spiritually reawakened site of a former Caern, a Shard Caern is formed. Margrave formed his faction around these Shard Seeds' cultivation (and control), cementing the formation of the Eastern Concordat. With the Dawn Tribes inherently possessing the means of creating and nurturing shard seeds of their own, the power the Western Concordat used to hold over these tribes rapidly unraveled, and the Western Concordat has found itself needing to cooperate and be diplomatic in ways that would have devolved into fighting in the past.<br /> <br /> The process of cleansing and reawakening a fallen Caern results in a Sept being able to be formed, but without a shard seed, the Caern cannot become more powerful than level 1. The area surrounding them is called a periphery, and shard seeds are planted to form a new heart. The elements and phases of planting the seed are similar to old building rites in that you have to prepare the land, clear it of threats, prepare extensive defenses, and then it begins. The ritemaster performs the Rite of the Furrowed Earth to plant the seed. If successful, the caern's old Patron is then capable of being summoned, extensive rites of contrition and chiminage performed. As a final step, the Rite of Acceptance is performed, binding the Patron to the Shard Seed. This part of the rite summons a storm of banes, though at a stage where the Patron can help with the defenses. The shard seed germinates if successful, and a new Shard Caern is formed. The Kahaila believe that with time and vigilant defense, the shard caerns can eventually grow in power to become a Great Caern once more, though being only ten years since the battle of Crescent Moon, none have yet grown to this point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T03:11:09-07:00","id":1542899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542859#post1542859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old Caern-building rites have effectively become bane-summoning rites from start to finish, making the creation of new caerns (called Great Caerns in this setting) more or less impossible. A shard caern is so-named after its heart, which is little more than a spiritual sliver taken from the heart of one of the 13 remaining Great Caerns. They are weaker and far more vulnerable to attack but retain the same abilities and powers reflecting the Great Caern that provided the shard.<br /> <br /> Kahaila, the Native American Ao, have returned. With the awakening of Turtle came their reawakening with it, each of them following a dream that jolted each of them awake of Gaia's Heart, a long-extinct gnostic flower believed to bridge the physical and spiritual world naturally. They, in turn, began seeking and awakening Hatha, Native American black bears of the Dawn Tribes who possess the means to heal the land and bring fossilized flora and fauna back to life. The Gurahl understood their duty from Gaia as her healers and began reluctantly restoring communication with both the Dawn Tribes and the Children of Gaia. Margrave Josef Konietzko saw an opportunity to form a new faction, and while other tribes were still reeling from the Sundering of their Caerns, threw the full might of the Shadow Lords' support behind the Children of Gaia to launch a go-for-broke expedition deep into Pangaea to recover a specimen of this plant.<br /> <br /> In short, they succeeded. They recovered the flower, a trillium-like plant called Gaia's Heart, from fossils from the Middle Devonian Epoch, when bones first appeared. This is from a time when Gaia was so powerful; she held an omniscient awareness of her realm, and the entire Gaian Realm was as spiritually charged as a caern, held together in a fine mycelial network connecting these delicate plants. Even in Pangaea, they managed to recover a single fossilized specimen. It was enough. They were able to bring it back to life, and upon planting it on a Great Caern's bawn and carefully tending it with ancient rites, it bloomed and began producing Shard Seeds.<br /> <br /> When planted and cared for in this manner, Shard Seeds produce more Gaia's Heart flowers. When grown in a cleansed and spiritually reawakened site of a former Caern, a Shard Caern is formed. Margrave formed his faction around these Shard Seeds' cultivation (and control), cementing the formation of the Eastern Concordat. With the Dawn Tribes inherently possessing the means of creating and nurturing shard seeds of their own, the power the Western Concordat used to hold over these tribes rapidly unraveled, and the Western Concordat has found itself needing to cooperate and be diplomatic in ways that would have devolved into fighting in the past.<br /> <br /> The process of cleansing and reawakening a fallen Caern results in a Sept being able to be formed, but without a shard seed, the Caern cannot become more powerful than level 1. The area surrounding them is called a periphery, and shard seeds are planted to form a new heart. The elements and phases of planting the seed are similar to old building rites in that you have to prepare the land, clear it of threats, prepare extensive defenses, and then it begins. The ritemaster performs the Rite of the Furrowed Earth to plant the seed. If successful, the caern's old Patron is then capable of being summoned, extensive rites of contrition and chiminage performed. As a final step, the Rite of Acceptance is performed, binding the Patron to the Shard Seed. This part of the rite summons a storm of banes, though at a stage where the Patron can help with the defenses. The shard seed germinates if successful, and a new Shard Caern is formed. The Kahaila believe that with time and vigilant defense, the shard caerns can eventually grow in power to become a Great Caern once more, though being only ten years since the battle of Crescent Moon, none have yet grown to this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a little too JRPG for myself, for my own Chronicles I'd probably go with reawakening Caerns through investing time and resources reinvigorating the Bawn, bringing songlines connected to the key Dreamings of the sacred site back to prominence and/or sacrificing items/people/resonance in line with the Caerns purpose in order to coax it from slumber.<br /> <br /> Will still be picking up WtE though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T06:01:48-07:00","id":1542904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542859#post1542859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that making reclaiming Caern without a shard seed is merely going to be very draining on the limited resources and wolfpower the garou have that most of time it's doubtful the effort was worth it in the first place. The fact that most Caern creation ritual is bane bait is a surprise to me.<br /> <br /> Like if things was that dire then its a matter of time before the garou and the killi will go extinct and the fact that expedition teamed returned with the means to semi reliably reclaim a lost Caern is seen as a miracle for the garou and undoability ensured the the formation of the Eastern Concordat.<br /> <br /> If nothing else all the members of the expedition will be remembered as the savors of Gaia for ages to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-30-2024, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T21:23:36-07:00","id":1542944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1542899#post1542899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its a little too JRPG for myself, for my own Chronicles I'd probably go with reawakening Caerns through investing time and resources reinvigorating the Bawn, bringing songlines connected to the key Dreamings of the sacred site back to prominence and/or sacrificing items/people/resonance in line with the Caerns purpose in order to coax it from slumber.<br /> <br /> Will still be picking up WtE though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a viable way to go about it, and I can see how that can form a major story arc for a pack to go through the paces of nourishing a Shard Caern into a Great Caern!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T20:36:37-07:00","id":1543046,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27167_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27167\" data-vbnamecard=\"27167\">mundusartis</a> I've noticed that two native American tribes older and younger brothers ( renamed Hapil and Kalaril in WtE) and the Hearthbound have actually fallen in with the Dawn tribes. For the former two I understand since the Dawn Tribes are big on protecting native rights and decolanizing they lands which would make them attractive to the garou tribes that has the strongest connection to Native American culture. I didn't expect the Hearthbound to be amoung the Dawn Tribes instead if say the Eastcons since I got the impression that they influence is a important factor that make the alliance possible in the frist place. I guess it's due to some kind of political shannagains that prevents the Hearthbound from Associating directly with the Eastcons though it doesn't really chance since I got the impression that Eastcons still have a close relations with Dawn Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T20:00:22-07:00","id":1544065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1540089#post1540089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to offer an idea what Werewolf the Essentials is; It takes the divided Nation from the BNS WtA book and builds upon it. It includes the Bitten, but so they do not override other breeds.<br /> <br /> The focus, as a direct challenge to W5, is of community and unity.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does BNS mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T21:57:37-07:00","id":1544074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1543046#post1543046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't expect the Hearthbound to be amoung the Dawn Tribes instead if say the Eastcons since I got the impression that they influence is a important factor that make the alliance possible in the frist place. I guess it's due to some kind of political shannagains that prevents the Hearthbound from Associating directly with the Eastcons though it doesn't really chance since I got the impression that Eastcons still have a close relations with Dawn Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to understand this outcome, one has to both consider the means through which one majority population violently subjugates a minority population and then consider this is something the Garou Nation has done many, many, many times before in the past. In short, Hapil recognized the Hearthbound being hunted and killed using the same means used against them in the Age of Storms, and again on the Changing Breeds in the Age of Tragedy during the War of Rage. To stand by and let it happen would make them no less complicit in genocide than the rest of the Western Concordiat. They saw a kinship in their struggle for survival and adopted them. To this day, Hapil act as elder surrogates to the Hearthbound, as the tribe hasn't existed long enough to have their own elders.<br /> <br /> The second consideration to be made is that when one examines the relationship Hapil hold with both their Kinfolk and crinos is the very standard by which Hearthbound hold other Tribes to. Since the beginning, Hapil Kinfolk hold rank and renown along with their Garou kin. Their being shapeshifters isn't status in and of itself. Likewise, this is a tribe whose crinos all fairly earned their ranks. Even if many crinos don't endure their extensive trials to pass their Rites of Passage, their elders are still always due their respect regardless of breed.<br /> <br /> The third consideration here is in the manner in which Hapil teach one another. It is lupus teaching homids, and homids teaching lupus. This tradition is carried over to the Hearthbound, where perspectives are shared in the upbringing and training process every Hearthbound undergoes.<br /> <br /> Finally, although the Eastcons now work with the Hearthbound, it didn't start that way. With the Shadow Lords, the Lazarite Movement did a lot of legwork to bring equity to their tribe, and the secret society came out as early allies to the Hearthbound, teaching them how to hide in the open. Bone Gnawers, Black Furies, and the Children of Gaia have always had weirdly gender and bioessentialist views on their crinos despite being vocal allies to them. Its either something tied to requiring one be a particular gender to hold rank or learn certain rites or another putting their crinos on the front lines and giving them unfortunately short-lived careers as Garou. One only needs to look at their upper seats of power to see how few crinos hold high rank or Sept positions for it to start painting a less than glowing picture of the tribe.<br /> <br /> While the Eastcons are now allies, the Dawn Tribes are their home. Their dedication to helping Kalaril reawaken Turtle cemented their alliance with the Garou. With the other changing breeds, it can still be a little touch and go (to a Balam, a penitent Dog is still a Dog.) but as the series progresses so will their evolution as a tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1544065#post1544065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does BNS mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>This refers to Mind's Eye Theater: Werewolf the Apocalypse, published by <b>B</b>y <b>N</b>ight <b>S</b>tudios in 2013. BNS Werewolf for short!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T16:30:23-07:00","id":1544935,"title":"","content":"Since WtE is going to release in two days of this post if everything goes according to plan. Anyone wants to share they thoughts on the current preview material available to you guys and genurally how WtE lore contrast with W5? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T07:42:52-07:00","id":1544974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1544935#post1544935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since WtE is going to release in two days of this post if everything goes according to plan. Anyone wants to share they thoughts on the current preview material available to you guys and genurally how WtE lore contrast with W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has actually been delayed to 17th of November.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-29T17:30:35-07:00","id":1545020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview?p=1544974#post1544974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has actually been delayed to 17th of November.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah that's unfortunate<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I wish the best for the team, and I hope they have smoother lunch than Bloodlines 2<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Well I think we should still think we should talk about how WtE lore contrast with W5 . <br /> <br /> <br /> Like take how Albrecht was portrayed in both products, like in Shattered nation basically just gives up after a bad fight with the spirals and just let the nation collapsed (and it isnt that bad of a fight since the simple of them killing Zhyzhak would at least let the garou spin it as a pyrrhic victory) while the Albrecht of WtE basically sacrificed him self to stop Storm bringer thus limiting the Apocalypse to <i>just </i>all but 13 of the cearns in North America blowing up and all the rituals that's need to create new cearns becoming bane bait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T00:01:58-07:00","id":1545089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1